    basic: "Pick up early to win later! If you are the Defender and the attack is 'Small' (Low numbers), it's often better to intentionally pick up those cards. This fills your hand with cards that allow you to defend better later, and it 'Starves' the attackers of the chance to throw in their high-value trumps. In Durak, a large hand of low cards is sometimes better than a small hand of high cards because of the throw-in mechanic.",
    intermediate: "The 'Podkidnoy' Trap: As an Attacker, don't throw in your cards immediately. Wait for the Defender to play a trump. If they play a Trump 9, and you have a Heart 9 in your hand, throw it in. You are forcing them to waste a SECOND trump to beat it. Exhausting the Defender's trumps is the fastest way to make them pick up.",
    advanced: "Card Counting (The Trump Count): Since there are only 9 cards per suit, and you know the dealer's trump card at the bottom, you can calculate almost exactly how many trumps are in play. In the late-game (when the deck is empty), if you know the Defender doesn't have the Ace of Trump, you can lead your King with absolute confidence. Focus on saving at least one high trump for the final '1-on-1' showdown.",
